## Reviewer points not followed

- Zero-width “blank” lines are in the Korean source, not only in the Indonesian. Deleting them fails the block checker. They are blog residue shared with the source, not an Indonesian-only defect.
- Q16–Q20 are body lines in the Korean and English articles as well. Turning them into headings would change the heading-level sequence.
- Heading “7” after “5” is the source outline. Changing it to 6 changes a counted digit.
- The difficulty table row cannot be removed without changing the table-row count. The cells were rewritten so they no longer read as an easy dismissal or an easy severance.
- One clause per paragraph in 005, 006, 008, 009, 013, and 015 matches the Korean block count. Merging them would fail the checker. Broken joins inside 013 were repaired without merging blocks.
- The suggested sentence “Konsultasi dalam bahasa Indonesia tidak disediakan” matches the forbidden-phrase rule that flags “konsultasi … bahasa Indonesia” as an offer of Indonesian consultation. The negative formula already used in 013 was used instead.
- English institution strings in the bios cannot be deleted: guidance-team-bios.test.ts requires “Ministry of Education, Legal Affairs Division”, “Legal Aid Foundation, Taichung Branch”, and “TWD 1.57M” byte-identical. Indonesian was added around those strings.
